# Regenerable training outputs: excluded from the repo / HPC clone because the
# retrain rewrites them. reports/metrics/ (small authoritative result CSVs,
# ~80 KB) is kept and tracked; reports/models/ is already covered by models/.
reports/figures/
reports/results/

# =============================================================================
# Data (Large files)
# =============================================================================
# NOTE: data/ (CFD CSV ground truth, ~1.4 GB) is tracked ON PURPOSE so a plain
# `git clone` brings everything needed to retrain on the HPC. If the clone is
# too large for your remote, untrack it (`git rm -r --cached data`) and copy it
# over with rsync/scp instead.
#
# The Overleaf paper bundle is not needed on the HPC and is excluded:
CABG_Paper.zip
*.zip


# =============================================================================
# Documentation / Papers (Not for GitHub)
# =============================================================================
doc/
# PINN-side change-index report for Overleaf transfer. Already covered by
# doc/ above; listed explicitly (incl. a bare-name rule) so the working
# report is never tracked even if moved out of doc/.
doc/CABG_Paper/PINN_CHANGES_FOR_OVERLEAF.md
PINN_CHANGES_FOR_OVERLEAF.md

